  <Markdown>
## The Testing Effect

Students who tested themselves recalled approximately **50% more**
material after one week compared to those who simply re-read the
material (Roediger &amp; Karpicke, 2006).

This finding — known as the *testing effect* — demonstrates that
retrieval practice strengthens memory more effectively than passive
review, even when learners feel less confident during practice.
